WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.690
You know, I've seen God
do some amazing things.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.370
And I don't mean just
in my life, right?

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.050
I've seen God do some amazing
things in other people's lives.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.210
I have seen the blessings.

5
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:15.770
I have seen God just
heal, miraculously

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.250
heal. I have seen God do things

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.170
that are too good to not believe.

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.770
And I love those moments.

9
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.970
Those are what I call the
extraordinary moments.

10
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.410
And they are special.

11
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.110
Why? Because they
are extraordinary.

12
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.870
They are beyond what we
can think or imagine.

13
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.490
And God has those moments and
you're gonna have those moments.

14
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.230
But here's what I
don't want you to miss.

15
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.430
I don't want you to miss the
ordinary moments with God.

16
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.650
If your life becomes
consumed with trying to chase

17
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.210
maybe what you call those
mountaintop moments, those

18
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.690
extraordinary experiences, and
you're constantly searching for

19
00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.290
the next thing that's just
gonna make you feel like you're

20
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:10.230
standing right there, there's
nothing wrong with those moments.

21
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.040
But when your life

22
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.570
becomes the pursuit

23
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.590
of those moments,

24
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.510
you miss God

25
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.500
in the ordinary
moments of every day.

26
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:30.553
What if your perspective was
about stacking ordinary moments

27
00:01:30.603 --> 00:01:35.433
with God, stacking and stacking
and stacking those ordinary

28
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:39.813
moments until they became
an extraordinary life?

29
00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:42.543
Lord, that's what we want.

30
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:45.263
We just want an extraordinary
life, which doesn't mean that

31
00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:49.583
we're going to be like rich
and famous and have status and

32
00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:50.703
significance, Lord.

33
00:01:50.753 --> 00:01:51.883
It's not about that.

34
00:01:52.653 --> 00:01:55.483
An extraordinary life
is one full of shalom.

35
00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:59.083
It's one that is fully and deeply
connected to you, God, that

36
00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:03.883
we're living into godly
purpose for our lives.

37
00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.293
And Lord, that's what we
are seeking today, Lord.

38
00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:10.173
And we just want to
overflow with your hope.

39
00:02:10.223 --> 00:02:13.373
And so, God, thank you that you
continue to fill us with your

40
00:02:13.423 --> 00:02:16.893
joy and your peace, your shalom,
and that through those things,

41
00:02:16.943 --> 00:02:21.533
God, the overflow of our
hope might draw someone

42
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:22.733
else close to you.

43
00:02:22.783 --> 00:02:24.666
In Jesus' name, amen.
